23. What is Semantic Search?
Traditional keyword search may focus heavily on exact terms.

Semantic search tries to retrieve information based on meaning using representations such as embeddings.

Example:

Document:
"A customer may cancel their subscription at any time."

Query:
"How can I terminate my plan?"

A semantic system can recognize that these are related even though the exact words differ.
