10. Why CNNs are useful?
Suppose you flatten a huge image and give every pixel directly to a fully connected network.

There could be a massive number of parameters.

CNNs use:
Local connectivity
A neuron looks at a local region.
Parameter sharing
The same filter can be applied across different parts of the image.

This makes CNNs much more practical for visual pattern detection.
11. Pooling
CNNs may also use pooling to reduce spatial dimensions.

For example:
Large feature map
       ↓
