       ↓
Smaller feature map

Max pooling takes the largest value in a local region.

Benefits can include:
- Reducing computation
- Reducing spatial dimensions
- Retaining strong detected features
Modern architectures sometimes use alternatives such as strided convolutions or global pooling instead.
